-- -*- mode: lua -*-

-- Launchpad map, Albert Gräf <agggraef@gmail.com>, 2 April 2024

-- IMPORTANT: In contrast to the other controllers, this device needs to be
-- connected to its own MIDI port, port #3, on *both* input and output.

-- NOTE: This has only been tested on the Launchpad Pro MK3 so far, so the
-- Launchpad Mini and X might still need some work, and you might have to
-- remap some buttons. As far as I know, the fader and drumrack setups
-- provided by the driver only work on the Launchpad Pro MK3. On the other
-- devices, similar functionality is available through custom layouts, but
-- you'll have to set these up using the Novation Components software.

-- This fader setup largely mimics the Launch Control XL map, with the faders
-- and knobs of the XL on the Launchpad's Volume and Pan/Sends/Device fader
-- pages. The CC numbers have been chosen to be compatible (see the Lua table
-- below for the actual numbers if you want to use these for a custom
-- Launchpad layout).

-- Volume (corresponding to the Launch Control XL faders): 1 = pitch hi,
-- 2 = pitch lo, 3 = pattern mode (random, up, down, etc.), 4 = pos/anacrusis
-- (the "scrubbing" control), 5 = tempo, 6 = meter numerator, 7 = meter
-- denominator, 8 = division.

-- The "knobs": Pan (Pan/Device on the XL) = bipolar mod controls,
-- Sends/Device (Send A/B on the XL) = min/max controls.

-- The resulting mapping of fader pages 1-4 of the Launchpad Pro MK3 is as
-- follows:

-- [hi]     [lo]   [mode] [pos]     [tempo] [num]     [denom] [divis]
-- [velmod] [pmod] [gain] [gatemod] [hmod]  [prefmod] [smod]  [nmod]
-- [minvel] [pmin] [wmin] [gate]    [hmin]  [pref]    [smin]  [uniq]
-- [maxvel] [pmax] [wmax] [gate]    [hmax]  [pref]    [smax]  [nmax]

-- Other functions are accessible using the launch grid in the session view
-- (accessible using the Session button at the top). This should work on all
-- variations of the Launchpad. The pre-assigned functions are color-coded and
-- laid out in the two pad rows at the bottom (note the additional loop prev
-- and next buttons in the bottom rows;on the XL these functions are on the
-- Send Select buttons):

--   - voice controls -                       - looper controls -
-- [mute] [latch] [bypass]  [      ] [      ] [load] [save] [loop]
--                [raptor]  [rewind]          [prev] [next] [play]

-- NB: On the Launchpad Pro MK3, the mute, latch, and bypass toggles are also
-- accessible using the Mute, Solo, and Record Arm hardware buttons at the
-- bottom (see below).

-- PAD CONTROLS: The pads on the launch grid have a sensitivity threshold; a
-- medium touch will trigger them, while a light touch just displays the
-- current binding and value (if any) in the console window.

-- INTELLIGENT MAPPING: The pads can be mapped using MIDI learn, in which case
-- they will light up to indicate that they are bound to a Raptor control. The
-- exact behavior of each pad depends on the type of control it is mapped to.
-- For toggled controls, it acts like a toggle button. Otherwise, it works
-- like a latching fader which inputs a value depending on the velocity (if it
-- is above the threshold) and snaps back to 0 (or the middle position, in the
-- case of a bipolar control) as soon as the pad is released.

-- HARDWARE BUTTONS: The Launchpad's hardware buttons positioned around the
-- launch grid will also be lit up. Some of them can also be MIDI-mapped. The
-- precise set of hardware buttons that you have depends on your type of
-- device, though, so some functions may not be available. Here is a brief
-- rundown of the available functions:

-- The Play and Capture MIDI buttons, if available, are bound to Raptor's play
-- and loop functions. If you don't have these then you can use the
-- corresponding pads in the session view instead (see above).

-- The left and right arrow buttons can be used to select the current Raptor
-- instance, while the up and down arrow buttons change presets. These are
-- only accessible in the session and drumrack views.

-- On the Launchpad Pro MK3, instances can also be selected using the upper
-- button row at the bottom, and the bottommost row has the following
-- functions:

-- Record Arm/Mute/Solo: These double as bypass/mute/latch toggles, which are
-- also on the launch grid (see above).

-- Volume/Pan/Sends/Device: Access the four fader pages (see above). A click
-- of the button activates the corresponding fader page. Another click on the
-- same button then returns you to the most previous (non-fader) vie. You can
-- also press and *hold* the button to momentarily switch to the fader page,
-- so that you can quickly change some faders, and revert to the previous view
-- as soon as your release the button again.

-- Stop Clip: Toggle between the standard note view and the drumrack view.

{
  -- alternative bindings for the mute/latch/bypass controls, uses the mute,
  -- solo, and record arm hardware buttons in the bottom row
  [1] = { [33] = { "bypass", true } },
  [2] = { [33] = { "mute", true } },
  [3] = { [33] = { "latch", true } },
  -- send / send A (min value) faders
  [13] = { [37] = "minvel" },
  [14] = { [37] = "pmin" },
  [15] = { [37] = "wmin" },
  [16] = { [37] = "gate" },
  [17] = { [37] = "hmin" },
  [18] = { [37] = "pref" },
  [19] = { [37] = "smin" },
  [20] = { [37] = "uniq" },
  -- device / send B (max value) faders
  [29] = { [37] = "maxvel" },
  [30] = { [37] = "pmax" },
  [31] = { [37] = "wmax" },
  [32] = { [37] = "gate" },
  [33] = { [37] = "hmax" },
  [34] = { [37] = "pref" },
  [35] = { [37] = "smax" },
  [36] = { [37] = "nmax" },
  -- pan (bipolar mod) faders
  [49] = { [37] = "velmod" },
  [50] = { [37] = "pmod" },
  [51] = { [37] = "gain" },
  [52] = { [37] = "gatemod" },
  [53] = { [37] = "hmod" },
  [54] = { [37] = "prefmod" },
  [55] = { [37] = "smod" },
  [56] = { [37] = "nmod" },
  -- volume faders
  [77] = { [37] = "pitchhi" },
  [78] = { [37] = "pitchlo" },
  [79] = { [37] = "mode" },
  [80] = { [37] = "pos" },
  [81] = { [37] = "tempo" },
  [82] = { [37] = "meter-num" },
  [83] = { [37] = "meter-denom" },
  [84] = { [37] = "division" },
  -- predefined pads (session view)
  -- 139, 140 unassigned
  [141] = { [33] = { "raptor", true } },
  [142] = { [33] = { "rewind", true } },
  -- 143 unassigned
  [144] = { [33] = { "loop-prev", true } },
  [145] = { [33] = { "loop-next", true } },
  [146] = { [33] = { "play", true } },
  -- 2nd row
  [149] = { [33] = { "mute", true } },
  [150] = { [33] = { "latch", true } },
  [151] = { [33] = { "bypass", true } },
  -- 152, 153 unassigned
  [154] = { [33] = { "loop-load", true } },
  [155] = { [33] = { "loop-save", true } },
  [156] = { [33] = { "loop", true } },
}
